  "assumptions": [
    "This is a synthetic 15-day held-out case sliced from the synthetic 30-day traffic trace; no operator traffic is represented.",
    "Days 0–14 of the source trace form the training/calibration window for the static comparator; days 15–29 form the held-out evaluation window.",
    "Static assignment selects cell-east and cell-north from the training window's sum of priority-weighted critical excess; this assignment is frozen for all 15 holdout days.",
    "Two virtual beams and 10 Mbps useful critical-excess capacity per beam are available in every daily interval.",
    "Each assigned beam serves min(cell critical excess, 10 Mbps). A selected cell with less than 10 Mbps of critical excess uses only its available excess.",
    "Critical excess is calculated for every cell, including unselected cells, as max(offered load minus terrestrial available capacity, 0).",
    "offset_s is relative to the held-out evaluation window; source_offset_s identifies the original 30-day trace offset.",
    "The two policies use identical held-out cell loads, cell priorities, beam count, beam capacity, time windows and arithmetic; no policy is given a larger physical model or resource budget.",
    "This is a deterministic scheduling comparison only; no radio propagation, SINR, interference, spectrum, HAPS positioning, wind, backhaul, edge compute, energy or flight operation is modeled.",
    "The result is a synthetic control baseline, not a reproduction of the Mbarek et al. 2026 real-operator-trace experiment."
  ]
